# ADR 299: Standardize Authentication Middleware for Journal Management Controllers

## Context

Journal management controllers handle sensitive user data and operations. Authentication middleware must be consistently applied across all controllers in the ManageJournals domain to prevent unauthorized access.

## Decision

All controllers within `app/Domains/Vault/ManageJournals/Web/Controllers` MUST apply authentication middleware to protect routes from unauthorized access.

## Implementation

- Apply `auth` middleware to all controller methods or use route groups
- Verify middleware is registered in the controller constructor or route definitions
- Test that unauthenticated requests receive 401/403 responses
- Document any exceptions with explicit reasoning

## Compliance

Code review must verify authentication middleware presence before merging changes to this domain.
